.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT OR Apache-2.0
.TH ZTOP 1 "November 2026" "zTop 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ztop \- a lightweight system monitor for macOS and Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ztop
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ztop
is a lightweight system monitor that displays CPU, memory, disk, and network
usage in real time. It runs as a local agent that collects metrics and
serves them over a secure, paired connection.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-port <PORT>
The port to listen on (default: 7102).
.TP
.B \-\-bind <ADDRESS>
The address to bind to (default: 127.0.0.1).
.TP
.B \-\-tls
Enable TLS (required for pairing).
.TP
.B \-\-pair
Enable pairing (required for remote access).
.TP
.B \-\-allow\-control
Allow paired clients to send signals and renice processes.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-advertise
Do not advertise the agent on the local network.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B agent
Run the zTop agent (default).
.TP
.B hub
Run the zTop hub (for managing multiple agents).
.SH EXAMPLES
Run the agent with TLS and pairing:
.PP
.nf
$ ztop agent \-\-tls \-\-pair
.fi
.PP
Run the agent with control enabled:
.PP
.nf
$ ztop agent \-\-tls \-\-pair \-\-allow\-control
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.config/ztop/
Configuration directory.
.TP
.B ~/.local/share/ztop/
Data directory (tokens, logs).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ztop\-hub (1),
.BR ztop\-agent (1)
.SH AUTHOR
zTop Maintainers <maintainers@ztop.dev>
